    "Q15": [
      { minScore: 0, maxScore: 4, text: "You indicate that you do not work with measurable annual goals (e.g. both financially and organizationally or with regard to product or market development). This doesn't seem very logical for a company of your size. Maybe it's time to start. This will have a clarifying and motivating effect and ensure growth. Good luck with the implementation." },
      { minScore: 5, maxScore: 6, text: "You do not yet formulate clear, measurable annual goals. The clearer and more measurably you formulate your goals (both financially and organizationally or with regard to product or market development), the higher the chance that you will also achieve those goals. This will have a clarifying and motivating effect and ensure growth. Given the size of your company, we recommend that you implement this as soon as possible." },
      { minScore: 7, maxScore: 8, text: "You are already working on formulating measurable annual goals - better late than never. The clearer and more measurably you formulate your goals (both financially and organizationally or with regard to product or market development), the higher the chance that you will also achieve those goals. This will have a clarifying and motivating effect and ensure growth." },
      { minScore: 9, maxScore: 10, text: "You have the process of measurable annual goals well under control. That's great. The clearer and more measurably you formulate your goals (both financially and organizationally or with regard to product or market development), the higher the chance that you will also achieve those goals. Keep it up!" },
    ],
    "Q16": [
      { minScore: 0, maxScore: 4, text: "You have no monthly or quarterly goals. Ouch, that's very unusual for a company of your size. Monthly or quarterly goals give you guidance and direction and ensure that you will achieve your annual goals. Think of them as \"small sprints\" that you have to win in order to achieve your annual goal. Fast growers are very disciplined in this process. You should start immediately." },
      { minScore: 5, maxScore: 6, text: "You have started setting measurable monthly or quarterly goals. Given the size of your company, it's important to continue to implement this quickly. After all, monthly or quarterly goals give you guidance and ensure that you will achieve your annual goals. Think of them as \"small sprints\" that you have to win in order to achieve your annual goal. Fast growers are very disciplined in this process." },
      { minScore: 7, maxScore: 8, text: "You have already come far with measurable monthly or quarterly goals. Monthly or quarterly goals give you guidance and direction and ensure that you will achieve your annual goals. Try making this into a regular process." },
      { minScore: 9, maxScore: 10, text: "You have the process of monthly and quarterly goals entirely under your thumb. That's good, because the fastest growers are very disciplined in this process." },
    ],
    "Q17": [
      { minScore: 0, maxScore: 4, text: "You do not yet have a business plan. Given the size of your company, it's about time you did. Establishing your goals, strategy and action plan can bring about a lot of clarity and teach you to anticipate certain challenges. When is the personnel planning done? What will the marketing strategy and the associated costs be? You have to make many difficult choices; a complete overview and plan will help you with this, including in the financial aspect." },
      { minScore: 5, maxScore: 6, text: "You have started putting together a business plan. Given the size of your company this seems quite late. Establishing your goals, strategy and action plan can bring about a lot of clarity and teach you to anticipate certain challenges. When should you hire someone? What will the marketing strategy be? You have to make many difficult choices; a complete overview and plan will help you with this, including in the financial aspect." },
      { minScore: 7, maxScore: 8, text: "You have already come far with working with a business plan; that's good. Establishing your goals, strategy and action plan can bring about a lot of clarity and teach you to anticipate certain challenges. When should you hire someone? What will the marketing strategy be? You have to make many difficult choices; a complete overview and plan will help you with this, including in the financial aspect." },
      { minScore: 9, maxScore: 10, text: "You have a well-thought-out business plan and are working with it. Establishing your goals, strategy and action plan can bring about a lot of clarity and teach you to anticipate certain challenges. That's the right approach to growing!" },
    ],
